Task 4: Privilege escalation
Now that we have a shell, let’s escalate our privileges to root.

Our next goal is to escalate our privileges and attain root access. To do this, we’ll search for files on the system with the SUID bit set that are owned by the root user. Files with the SUID bit, when run, inherit the owner’s permissions. So, if we discover a binary owned by root with the SUID bit, we might be able to use it to enhance our privileges.

Command: find / -user root –perm /4000 2>/dev/null

We are using 4000 as it is the permission for SUID.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

